nge factor essential for transport vesicle budding from the ER. Nature 365:347&#x02013;349 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8377826</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barlowe</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Orci</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Yeung</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hosobuchi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamamoto</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Salama</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Rexach</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Ravazzola</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Amherdt</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Schekman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>COPII: a membrane coat formed by Sec proteins that drive vesicle budding from the endoplasmic reticulum</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1994</year><volume>77</volume><fpage>895</fpage><lpage>907</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Barlowe C, Orci L, Yeung T, Hosobuchi M, Hamamoto S, Salama N, Rexach MF, Ravazzola M, Amherdt M, Schekman R (1994) COPII: a membrane coat formed by Sec proteins that drive vesicle budding from the endoplasmic reticulum. Cell 77:895&#x02013;907 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8004676</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barlowe</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Signals for COPII-dependent export from the ER: what&#x02019;s the ticket out?</article-title><source>Trends Cell Biol</source><year>2003</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>295</fpage><lpage>300</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Barlowe C (2003) Signals for COPII-depen